# =============================================================================
# @hc1com/design-system — .npmrc template
# =============================================================================
#
# Copy this file to `.npmrc` (which is .gitignored) and set your GitHub PAT to
# publish or install privately. The .npmrc that lives beside package.json is
# used by npm both for publishing (needs write:packages) AND for the local
# `npm install` step of dev (needs read:packages for private consumers).
#
# GENERATE A TOKEN
#   https://github.com/settings/tokens (classic)
#   Scopes required for PUBLISHING: write:packages + read:packages + repo
#   Scopes required for INSTALLING:  read:packages (+ repo if the pkg is private)
#
# USAGE — LOCAL PUBLISH
#   1. cp .npmrc.example .npmrc
#   2. export GITHUB_TOKEN=<paste your PAT here>
#   3. npm publish
#
# USAGE — CONSUMER APP INSTALL
#   Consumer app copies this same file to .npmrc, sets GITHUB_TOKEN in their
#   environment (or in their CI's secrets), and runs `npm install`.
#
# CI (this repo's Actions publish workflow) does NOT use this file — it
# configures the registry via actions/setup-node using GITHUB_TOKEN from
# secrets automatically.
# =============================================================================

@hc1com:registry=https://npm.pkg.github.com
//npm.pkg.github.com/:_authToken=${GITHUB_TOKEN}
